Title: RACOON RESCUE - V2
Credit: Scene Draft
Author: Scene Writer Agent
Draft date: January 2026

===

/* THE PROMETHEUS MOMENT - Danny discovers his "solution" */
/* Approximate page count: 1.5-2 pages */
/* Power arc: DEFEATED -> GOD */

EXT. DUSTY'S PARKING LOT - NIGHT

Sodium vapor lights paint everything the color of old bruises.
Orange. Sickly. The kind of light that makes everyone look
guilty of something.

DANNY VEGA's pickup sits alone in the far corner. A monument
to bad decisions waiting to happen.

INT. DANNY'S TRUCK - CONTINUOUS

Danny slumps behind the wheel. Keys in ignition. Engine silent.

His hand trembles as he lifts the BREATHALYZER INTERLOCK DEVICE
mounted to the steering column. Clinical black plastic. A
single red LED eye.

He blows.

BEEP. The LED pulses RED.

He wipes his mouth. Tries again. Longer. Controlled. Like
willpower alone can metabolize whiskey.

BEEP. RED.

Danny stares at the device. The device stares back. It doesn't
blink. It doesn't care. It has all night.

He slams both palms against the steering wheel.

Silence.

Danny's head drops. Forehead against the wheel. The posture of
a man who has run out of moves.

DANNY (V.O.)
Here's the thing about being drunk
that sober people don't get: every
idea feels like the best idea you've
ever had.

He stays there. Breathing. The truck's cabin suddenly too small,
too quiet, too much like a coffin.

Then--

Through the windshield: MOVEMENT. Something in the darkness
behind the bar.

Danny lifts his head.

EXT. DUSTY'S PARKING LOT - DANNY'S POV - CONTINUOUS

The DUMPSTER behind the restaurant sits in a pool of sodium
vapor light. A single overhead lamp illuminates it from above.

The effect is almost religious. A garbage cathedral. The
dumpster glows like something holy, something meant to be found.

The lid is cracked open. Something RUSTLES inside.

INT. DANNY'S TRUCK - CONTINUOUS

Danny watches. Curious despite himself. Or maybe because of
himself--the version of himself that exists at eight whiskeys
deep, when bad ideas feel like destiny.

He opens the door.

EXT. DUSTY'S PARKING LOT - CONTINUOUS

Danny walks toward the light. Gravel crunches under boots that
don't quite track straight.

The dumpster looms larger as he approaches. Behind it: the
neon glow of Dusty's beer signs. Arby's wrappers scattered
like confetti from a celebration no one remembers.

Danny stops three feet away. Peers over the edge.

EXT. DUMPSTER - DANNY'S POV - CONTINUOUS

Among the garbage, belly-up, surrounded by fast food debris
and fermenting vegetables:

A RACCOON.

Fat. Unconscious. One tiny paw TWITCHES occasionally--the
only sign of life. Its belly rises and falls with the slow
rhythm of the profoundly food-drunk.

The sodium vapor light catches its fur. Makes it glow. A
creature of the garbage, transformed by circumstance into
something almost beautiful.

EXT. DUSTY'S PARKING LOT - CONTINUOUS

Danny stares down at the raccoon.

The raccoon's paw twitches again. Then stillness.

Danny looks back at his truck. At the breathalyzer waiting
inside. At the red light that said no.

He looks down at the raccoon. At its small chest. Rising.
Falling. Rising. Falling.

Breathing.

CLOSE ON: Danny's face.

We watch it happen in real time. The worst idea of his life,
born in the orange glow of a parking lot at midnight.

His brow furrows. His eyes narrow. The corner of his mouth
twitches--not quite a smile, but something adjacent to one.

Recognition.

His head tilts. His lips part.

And there it is: the EUREKA. The terrible, beautiful eureka
of a drunk man who has just solved an unsolvable problem.

Danny straightens up. Looks down at the raccoon with new eyes.

No longer a creature. A tool. A solution. A way out.

DANNY
(quietly, almost reverent)
You breathe.

He reaches down.

FADE TO BLACK.

/* End scene - approximately 1.75 pages */
/* Note: The V.O. can be cut if we trust the visual storytelling */
/* The silence before "You breathe" should play like a held breath */
